SUMMARY:Funding 101: The Investment Landscape for Cleantech Entrepreneurs in Egypt
DESCRIPTION:A practical discussion for Egyptian cleantech entrepreneurs on what they need to finance\, which capital fits at each stage\, which funders to approach\, and what financial and non-financial support can help them move from prototype to commercial scale. \n \n At the end of the session\, an entrepreneur should be able to: \n\n-Assess the company's current stage and financing need: distinguish among capital for R&D\, validation\, first deployment\, working capital and scale. \n-Identify the right capital and funding source: match stage\, sector\, capital requirement and purpose to the most relevant instruments and recognize options that are unlikely to fit yet. \n-Distinguish a good business from a fit for a specific funder: understand how ticket size\, return model\, time horizon\, mandate\, risk appetite and repayment requirements shape the answer. \n-Understand what must be proven next: identify the minimum technical\, commercial\, financial and governance evidence needed to become eligible for the next stage of capital. \n-Use non-financial support strategically: recognize when technical assistance\, technical due diligence\, market intelligence\, policy support\, certification\, governance or customer access is needed to unlock finance.
CATEGORIES:CLEANTECH & CLIMATE INNOVATION
LOCATION:(ALX) Stage 01: The Great Hall\, Egypt
SEQUENCE:0
UID:45845f6030aa00625a8c51c45f9ed6cb
