SUMMARY:From Invention to Impact: Commercialising Intellectual Property
DESCRIPTION:Intellectual property can be one of the most valuable assets created by researchers\, entrepreneurs\, and technology companies but turning an invention into commercial value requires more guided efforts than commonly perceived. This panel explores how IP can be created\, protected\, valued\, licensed\, funded\, and transformed into products\, companies\, and commercial partnerships. Bringing together perspectives from research\, entrepreneurship\, and law\, the discussion will examine what it takes to move promising ideas from the lab or the founder’s desk into the market.
