SUMMARY:What They Failed to Teach in Venture: Valuation
DESCRIPTION:Valuation is one of the most debated topics in venture capital and one of the least understood. While traditional finance offers formulas and frameworks\, venture investors often operate in a world where data is limited\, uncertainty is high\, and outcomes are far from predictable.\nIn this session\, we'll explore what really drives startup valuations beyond spreadsheets and financial models. From founder quality and market potential to competitive dynamics\, and market cycles\, participants will gain a practical understanding of how valuation decisions are made in the real world. Through candid discussions and real venture examples\, this workshop will challenge common assumptions and reveal the nuances that rarely make it into textbooks\, pitch decks\, or investment memos.\n
